  "slug": "colored-indexes-832d",
  "summary": "New work dissects AlphaFold 3 and OpenFold internals and PLM representations while extending protein generation and design with structure-derived priors.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is mechanistic scrutiny of deep learning models for protein structure and sequence. AlphaInterp reports that a few divergent MSA homologues suffice to recover AlphaFold 3 structure, tied to pairformer latent geometry. A separate preprint probes OpenFold's 48 Evoformer layers with four decoders, tracking distance decodability, TM-score reconstruction, and triangle-inequality violations. A third preprint benchmarks ESMC interpretability against curated residue-level annotations, finding that conclusions depend on depth, probe, neuron and SAE choices. Alongside, generative and design models use structure- or sequence-derived priors: FoldMapper (structure-derived evolutionary profiles, multiscale graph encoder), MANTA (language-model geometric priors for IDP ensembles), and A2Holo (dual-stream flow matching for apo-to-holo transitions). New here is quantitative layer-wise probing rather than a shared algorithm.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
